# 19. CLIENT PORTAL MODULE

The Client Portal is a major component of this system and must receive special attention in both functionality and visual design.

It must be a separate, restricted client-facing experience.

Use a dedicated route such as:

`/client-portal`

The Client Portal must use the same central database and project records as the internal CBMS.

Do not create duplicate project records or a separate client project database.

## 19.1 Client account management

Allow administrators to:

- Create client accounts.
- Assign client accounts to companies.
- Assign one or multiple projects to a client.
- Create multiple representatives for one client company.
- Activate or deactivate accounts.
- Reset passwords.
- Manage client permissions.

A client must only see projects explicitly assigned to that client's account.

## 19.2 Client dashboard design

The Client Portal must be visually polished, professional, modern, and easy to understand.

It must not look like an accounting system or an internal administrative dashboard.

Use a premium construction project reporting experience.

Prioritize:

- Attractive project overview cards.
- Large circular progress indicators.
- Clear project status indicators.
- Phase progress bars.
- Construction timelines.
- Milestone tracking.
- Planned versus actual progress charts.
- Recent approved progress updates.
- Approved construction photo galleries.
- Clear expected completion information.

The design must be responsive and work well on mobile devices.

## 19.3 Client project overview

For each assigned project, show:

- Project name.
- Project reference.
- Project location.
- Project description.
- Start date.
- Expected completion date.
- Current project status.
- Overall completion percentage.
- Current construction phase.
- Current phase progress.
- Next milestone.
- Expected completion information.
- Authorized project manager contact.

The most important project information should be immediately visible without requiring the client to navigate through multiple pages.

## 19.4 Current construction phase

